<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Ferdinando, Duke of Genoa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1822">1822</a>–<a href="/years/1855">1855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinando, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, the second son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-albert-of-sardinia">Charles Albert of Sardinia</a>, who commanded troops in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a> in 1848–1849. In July 1848 the Sicilian parliament, having deposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>, elected him King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, but he declined the crown. His daughter Margherita became Queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div>
